Mocker engine for testing Dynamo LLM infrastructure with vLLM-style CLI.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
  --model-path MODEL_PATH
                        Path to model directory or HuggingFace model ID for
                        tokenizer
  --endpoint ENDPOINT   Dynamo endpoint string (default:
                        dyn://dynamo.backend.generate for aggregated/decode,
                        dyn://dynamo.prefill.generate for prefill)
  --model-name MODEL_NAME
                        Model name for API responses (default: derived from
                        model-path)
  --num-gpu-blocks-override NUM_GPU_BLOCKS
                        Explicit usable GPU-block capacity per data-parallel
                        rank for the mock KV cache. When unset, AIS-backed
                        mocker estimates the value; non-AIS mocker uses 16384.
  --block-size BLOCK_SIZE
                        Token block size for KV cache blocks. When unset, the
                        default depends on engine: vLLM 64, SGLang 1, TRTLLM
                        32.
  --max-model-len MAX_MODEL_LEN
                        Maximum sequence length, including prompt and
                        generated tokens. When omitted, no model-length limit
                        is enforced.
  --max-num-seqs MAX_NUM_SEQS
                        Maximum number of sequences per iteration (default:
                        256)
  --max-num-batched-tokens MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS
                        Maximum number of batched tokens per iteration
                        (default: 8192)
  --enable-prefix-caching
                        Enable automatic prefix caching (default: True)
  --no-enable-prefix-caching
                        Disable automatic prefix caching
  --enable-chunked-prefill
                        Enable chunked prefill (default: True)
  --no-enable-chunked-prefill
                        Disable chunked prefill
  --preemption-mode PREEMPTION_MODE
                        Preemption mode for decode eviction under memory
                        pressure. 'lifo' (default) evicts the newest request
                        (matches vLLM v1), 'fifo' evicts the oldest request.
  --speedup-ratio SPEEDUP_RATIO
                        Speedup ratio for mock execution (default: 1.0). Use 0
                        for infinite speedup (no simulation delays).
  --decode-speedup-ratio DECODE_SPEEDUP_RATIO
                        Additional speedup multiplier applied only to decode
                        steps (default: 1.0). Models speculative decoding
                        (e.g. Eagle) where decode throughput improves without
                        affecting prefill latency. Effective decode speedup is
                        speedup_ratio * decode_speedup_ratio.
  --data-parallel-size DP_SIZE
                        Number of data parallel replicas (default: 1)
  --startup-time STARTUP_TIME
                        Simulated engine startup time in seconds (default:
                        None)
  --planner-profile-data PLANNER_PROFILE_DATA
                        Path to profile results directory containing
                        selected_prefill_interpolation/ and
                        selected_decode_interpolation/ subdirectories
                        (default: None, uses hardcoded polynomials)
  --ais-perf-model, --aic-perf-model
                        Use AISimulate's perf model directly for latency
                        prediction. Requires aisimulate installed.
  --gpu-memory-utilization GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION
                        GPU memory fraction for AIS KV capacity estimation
                        with vLLM (default: 0.9).
  --mem-fraction-static MEM_FRACTION_STATIC
                        Static memory fraction for AIS KV capacity estimation
                        with SGLang (default: 0.88).
  --free-gpu-memory-fraction FREE_GPU_MEMORY_FRACTION
                        Fraction of free GPU memory (after model load) for the
                        KV cache, for AIS KV capacity estimation with TRT-LLM
                        (default: 0.9).
  --ais-system AIS_SYSTEM, --aic-system AIS_SYSTEM
                        AIS system name (e.g., 'h200_sxm'). Used with --ais-
                        perf-model.
  --ais-backend AIS_BACKEND, --aic-backend AIS_BACKEND
                        AIS backend name used for perf database lookups. When
                        unset, falls back to --engine-type. Set this to
                        decouple the AIS perf model from the simulated engine
                        type (e.g. simulate with vllm while using trtllm AIS
                        data).
  --ais-backend-version AIS_BACKEND_VERSION, --aic-backend-version AIS_BACKEND_VERSION
                        AIS performance-database version: 'current',
                        'previous', or 'next' when available, or a version
                        assigned to one of those slots. Defaults to the
                        release database's 'current' slot.
  --ais-tp-size AIS_TP_SIZE, --aic-tp-size AIS_TP_SIZE
                        Tensor parallel size for AIS latency prediction
                        (default: 1). Only affects AIS performance model
                        lookups, not mocker scheduling.
  --ais-moe-tp-size AIS_MOE_TP_SIZE, --aic-moe-tp-size AIS_MOE_TP_SIZE
                        MoE tensor-parallel size for AIS latency prediction.
                        Required for MoE models. Constraint: ais_tp_size *
                        ais_attention_dp_size == ais_moe_tp_size *
                        ais_moe_ep_size.
  --ais-moe-ep-size AIS_MOE_EP_SIZE, --aic-moe-ep-size AIS_MOE_EP_SIZE
                        MoE expert-parallel size for AIS latency prediction.
                        Required for MoE models. Constraint: ais_tp_size *
                        ais_attention_dp_size == ais_moe_tp_size *
                        ais_moe_ep_size.
  --ais-attention-dp-size AIS_ATTENTION_DP_SIZE, --aic-attention-dp-size AIS_ATTENTION_DP_SIZE
                        Attention data-parallel size for AIS latency
                        prediction (default: 1). Corresponds to the 'dp'
                        dimension in AIS CLI output.
  --ais-nextn AIS_NEXTN, --aic-nextn AIS_NEXTN
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] Number of MTP draft tokens to sample
                        (1-5).
  --ais-nextn-accept-rates AIS_NEXTN_ACCEPT_RATES, --aic-nextn-accept-rates AIS_NEXTN_ACCEPT_RATES
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] Comma-separated conditional MTP
                        acceptance rates. Entry i is P(draft i accepted | all
                        earlier drafts were accepted).
  --ais-mtp-seed AIS_MTP_SEED, --aic-mtp-seed AIS_MTP_SEED
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] Base RNG seed for mocker MTP burst
                        sampling.
  --num-workers NUM_WORKERS
                        Number of mocker workers to launch in the same process
                        (default: 1). All workers share the same tokio runtime
                        and thread pool.
  --ais-perf-config AIS_PERF_CONFIG
                        Complete ForwardPassPerfModelConfig as JSON or a
                        JSON/YAML file.
  --reasoning REASONING
                        Enable reasoning token output. JSON object with
                        fields: start_thinking_token_id (u32),
                        end_thinking_token_id (u32), thinking_ratio (0.0-1.0).
                        Example: '{"start_thinking_token_id": 123,
                        "end_thinking_token_id": 456, "thinking_ratio": 0.6}'
  --response-replay-trace-path RESPONSE_REPLAY_TRACE_PATH
                        Optional Mooncake JSONL trace containing
                        output_token_ids for output_replay_id annotation
                        lookup.
  --engine-type ENGINE_TYPE
                        Engine simulation type: 'vllm' (default), 'sglang', or
                        'trtllm'.
  --sglang-schedule-policy SGLANG_SCHEDULE_POLICY
                        SGLang scheduling policy: 'fifo' (default) or 'lpm'
                        (longest prefix match). The 'fcfs' alias is deprecated
                        and will be removed in Dynamo 1.8.0.
  --sglang-page-size SGLANG_PAGE_SIZE
                        Deprecated SGLang alias for --block-size; removed in
                        Dynamo 1.8.0. Ignored for other backends.
  --sglang-max-prefill-tokens SGLANG_MAX_PREFILL_TOKENS
                        SGLang maximum prefill tokens budget per batch
                        (default: 16384).
  --sglang-chunked-prefill-size SGLANG_CHUNKED_PREFILL_SIZE
                        SGLang chunked prefill size — max tokens per chunk
                        (default: 8192).
  --sglang-clip-max-new-tokens SGLANG_CLIP_MAX_NEW_TOKENS
                        SGLang clip max new tokens for admission budget
                        (default: 4096).
  --sglang-schedule-conservativeness SGLANG_SCHEDULE_CONSERVATIVENESS
                        SGLang schedule conservativeness factor 0.0-1.0
                        (default: 1.0).
  --sglang-generate     Serve native streaming SGLang /generate requests
                        (default: disabled).
  --systemone-serial    Enable the serial SystemOne profile: native SGLang,
                        aggregated, DP1, with scheduler max_num_seqs=1
                        (default: disabled).
  --trtllm-capacity-scheduler-policy TRTLLM_CAPACITY_SCHEDULER_POLICY
                        TRT-LLM capacity scheduler policy. v1 supports only
                        'guaranteed_no_evict' (default).
  --extra-engine-args EXTRA_ENGINE_ARGS
                        Path to JSON file with mocker configuration. If
                        provided, overrides individual CLI arguments.
  --disaggregation-mode {agg,prefill,decode}
                        Worker disaggregation mode: 'agg' (default,
                        aggregated), 'prefill' (prefill-only worker), or
                        'decode' (decode-only worker).
  --is-prefill-worker   DEPRECATED: use --disaggregation-mode=prefill.
                        Register as Prefill model type instead of
                        Chat+Completions (default: False)
  --is-decode-worker    DEPRECATED: use --disaggregation-mode=decode. Mark
                        this as a decode worker which does not publish KV
                        events (default: False)
  --zmq-kv-events-ports ZMQ_KV_EVENTS_PORTS
                        Comma-separated list of ZMQ PUB base ports for KV
                        event publishing in vLLM native wire format. One port
                        per worker (must match --num-workers). Each worker's
                        DP ranks bind on base_port + dp_rank. A
                        KvEventPublisher relay subscribes and forwards events
                        to NATS. (default: None, disabled)
  --zmq-replay-ports ZMQ_REPLAY_PORTS
                        Comma-separated list of ZMQ ROUTER base ports for KV
                        event replay. One port per worker (must match --num-
                        workers). Each worker's DP ranks bind on base_port +
                        dp_rank. Used alongside --zmq-kv-events-ports for gap
                        recovery. (default: None, disabled)
  --bootstrap-ports BOOTSTRAP_PORTS
                        Comma-separated list of bootstrap ports for
                        disaggregated serving rendezvous. One port per worker
                        (must match --num-workers). Prefill workers listen on
                        these ports; decode workers connect to them. If not
                        specified, bootstrap rendezvous is disabled.
  --kv-transfer-bandwidth KV_TRANSFER_BANDWIDTH
                        KV cache transfer bandwidth in GB/s for disaggregated
                        serving latency simulation. When unset, uses the
                        AISimulate engine default. Set to 0 to disable KV
                        transfer delay. For intra-node NVLink, typical value
                        is ~450.
  --kv-transfer-timing-mode KV_TRANSFER_TIMING_MODE
                        Physical KV footprint used for coordinated
                        disaggregated transfer timing.
  --kv-cache-dtype {auto,bfloat16,fp8,fp8_ds_mla,fp8_e4m3,fp8_e5m2,fp8_inc}
                        Data type for KV cache, used to compute
                        kv_bytes_per_token. 'auto' uses the model's dtype
                        (default).
  --kv-bytes-per-token KV_BYTES_PER_TOKEN
                        KV cache bytes per token. If not specified, auto-
                        computed from model config using: num_layers * 2 *
                        num_kv_heads * head_dim * dtype_bytes.
  --num-host-blocks NUM_HOST_BLOCKS
                        Enable native vLLM G2 (host) KV offload with this per-
                        DP-rank host cache capacity in blocks. Host blocks are
                        sized by --kv-bytes-per-token. Requires prefix
                        caching.
  --host-offload-d2h-bandwidth-gbps HOST_OFFLOAD_D2H_BANDWIDTH_GBPS
                        Per-DP-rank native G2 D2H bandwidth in decimal GB/s
                        (AISimulate default when unset; 0 is unlimited).
                        Requires --num-host-blocks.
  --host-offload-h2d-bandwidth-gbps HOST_OFFLOAD_H2D_BANDWIDTH_GBPS
                        Per-DP-rank native G2 H2D bandwidth in decimal GB/s
                        (AISimulate default when unset; 0 is unlimited).
                        Requires --num-host-blocks.
  --stagger-delay STAGGER_DELAY
                        Delay in seconds between launching each worker. Set to
                        0 to disable staggering (default). Use -1 for auto
                        mode (0.1s for 33-128 workers, 0.2s for >128 workers,
                        0 otherwise).
  --discovery-backend {kubernetes,etcd,file,mem}
                        Discovery backend: kubernetes (K8s API), etcd
                        (distributed KV), file (local filesystem), mem (in-
                        memory). Etcd uses the ETCD_* env vars (e.g.
                        ETCD_ENDPOINTS) for connection details. File uses root
                        dir from env var DYN_FILE_KV or defaults to
                        $TMPDIR/dynamo_store_kv.
  --request-plane {nats,tcp}
                        Determines how requests are distributed from routers
                        to workers. 'tcp' is fastest [nats|tcp]
  --response-plane {tcp,quic,velo}
                        Select the response transport. Frontend and workers
                        must match.
  --event-plane {nats,zmq}
                        Determines how events are published [nats|zmq]. If
                        unset, auto-detected from --discovery-backend (zmq for
                        file/mem, nats for etcd/kubernetes).

Router Options:
  --router-mode {round-robin,random,kv,direct,least-loaded,device-aware-weighted}
                        How to route the request. least-loaded routes to the
                        worker with the fewest active requests. device-aware-
                        weighted routes based on worker device type
                        (CPU/CUDA). In disaggregated prefill mode, least-
                        loaded skips bootstrap optimization and falls back to
                        the synchronous prefill path. env var: DYN_ROUTER_MODE
                        | default: None
  --router-session-affinity-ttl-secs SESSION_AFFINITY_TTL_SECS
                        Enable session affinity with this router-local idle
                        TTL in seconds. Bindings synchronize across router
                        replicas on a best-effort basis. Affinity is disabled
                        when this option is omitted. This is independent of KV
                        prediction TTL settings. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_SESSION_AFFINITY_TTL_SECS | default: None
  --router-session-affinity-mode {hard,soft}
                        How an existing session binding participates in worker
                        selection. hard makes the binding an exact constraint;
                        soft exposes it as a policy-visible preference. env
                        var: DYN_ROUTER_SESSION_AFFINITY_MODE | default: hard
  --active-decode-blocks-threshold ACTIVE_DECODE_BLOCKS_THRESHOLD
                        Threshold fraction (0.0-1.0) of KV cache block
                        utilization above which a worker is considered busy.
                        Setting a numeric value enables this rejection check.
                        Unset by default; pass 'None' to disable it. env var:
                        DYN_ACTIVE_DECODE_BLOCKS_THRESHOLD | default: None
  --active-prefill-tokens-threshold ACTIVE_PREFILL_TOKENS_THRESHOLD
                        Deprecated; will be removed in v1.7. Use --active-
                        prefill-tokens-threshold-frac. Literal token count
                        threshold for determining when a worker is considered
                        busy based on prefill token utilization. When active
                        prefill tokens exceed this threshold, the worker is
                        marked as busy. Setting a numeric value enables this
                        rejection check. Unset by default; pass 'None' to
                        disable it. Uses OR logic with --active-prefill-
                        tokens-threshold-frac. env var:
                        DYN_ACTIVE_PREFILL_TOKENS_THRESHOLD | default: None
  --active-prefill-tokens-threshold-frac ACTIVE_PREFILL_TOKENS_THRESHOLD_FRAC
                        Fraction of max_num_batched_tokens for busy detection.
                        Worker is busy when active_prefill_tokens > frac *
                        max_num_batched_tokens. Setting a numeric value
                        enables this rejection check. Unset by default; pass
                        'None' to disable it. Uses OR logic with --active-
                        prefill-tokens-threshold. env var:
                        DYN_ACTIVE_PREFILL_TOKENS_THRESHOLD_FRAC | default:
                        None

KV Router Options:
  --load-aware, --no-load-aware
                        --load-aware is deprecated and will be removed in
                        v1.7; use the load-only policy and router tracking
                        settings in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Enable
                        the load-aware routing preset. On the frontend, this
                        implies --router-mode kv. This preset sets
                        overlap_score_credit=0, disables KV events and KV-
                        reuse assumptions, enables active-block and prefill-
                        token load tracking, and disables remote/shared cache
                        indexers. The builtin policy does not request cache
                        inputs in this mode. env var: DYN_ROUTER_LOAD_AWARE |
                        default: False
  --router-kv-overlap-score-credit OVERLAP_SCORE_CREDIT
                        --router-kv-overlap-score-credit is deprecated and
                        will be removed in v1.7; use overlap_score_credit in
                        the default policy parameters in --router-policy-
                        config. KV Router: Credit multiplier for device-local
                        prefix overlap. Must be finite and non-negative;
                        values above 1.0 give device overlap extra credit,
                        with adjusted prefill cost clamped at zero. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_KV_OVERLAP_SCORE_CREDIT | default: 1.0
  --router-kv-overlap-score-credit-decay OVERLAP_SCORE_CREDIT_DECAY
                        --router-kv-overlap-score-credit-decay is deprecated
                        and will be removed in v1.7; use
                        overlap_score_credit_decay in the default policy
                        parameters in --router-policy-config. KV Router: Decay
                        rate for device-local overlap credit as active prefill
                        load rises above the least-loaded eligible worker. 0
                        disables decay; 1 halves credit at one request-
                        equivalent of excess active prefill load. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_KV_OVERLAP_SCORE_CREDIT_DECAY | default:
                        0.0
  --router-prefill-load-scale PREFILL_LOAD_SCALE
                        --router-prefill-load-scale is deprecated and will be
                        removed in v1.7; use prefill_load_scale in the default
                        policy parameters in --router-policy-config. KV
                        Router: Scale applied to adjusted prompt-side prefill
                        load after overlap and lower-tier cache-hit credits
                        are subtracted. env var: DYN_ROUTER_PREFILL_LOAD_SCALE
                        | default: 1.0
  --router-decode-active-request-weight DECODE_ACTIVE_REQUEST_WEIGHT
                        --router-decode-active-request-weight is deprecated
                        and will be removed in v1.7; use
                        decode_active_request_weight in the default policy
                        parameters in --router-policy-config. [EXPERIMENTAL]
                        KV Router: Block-equivalent decode cost added for each
                        active request on a candidate worker. Use this to
                        balance decode batch size when step latency depends
                        more on request count than resident KV footprint. Must
                        be finite and non-negative. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_DECODE_ACTIVE_REQUEST_WEIGHT | default: 0.0
  --router-host-cache-hit-weight HOST_CACHE_HIT_WEIGHT
                        KV Router: Credit multiplier for host-pinned (CPU
                        offload) prefix overlap. Range: 0.0 to 1.0; higher
                        values more strongly prefer workers holding the prefix
                        in CPU-tier KV cache. Symmetric to --router-kv-
                        overlap-score-credit but applied to host_pinned tier
                        overlap. env var: DYN_ROUTER_HOST_CACHE_HIT_WEIGHT |
                        default: 0.75
  --router-disk-cache-hit-weight DISK_CACHE_HIT_WEIGHT
                        KV Router: Credit multiplier for disk/lower-tier (e.g.
                        NVMe-backed) prefix overlap. Range: 0.0 to 1.0. Same
                        semantics as --router-host-cache-hit-weight applied to
                        the disk tier. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_DISK_CACHE_HIT_WEIGHT | default: 0.25
  --router-temperature ROUTER_TEMPERATURE
                        --router-temperature is deprecated and will be removed
                        in v1.7; use router_temperature in the default policy
                        parameters in --router-policy-config. KV Router:
                        Temperature for normalized worker sampling via
                        softmax. Higher values promote more randomness, and 0
                        falls back to deterministic. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_TEMPERATURE | default: 0.0
  --router-kv-events, --no-router-kv-events, --kv-events, --no-kv-events
                        KV Router: Enable/disable KV events. Use --router-kv-
                        events to enable (default, router receives cache state
                        events from workers) or --no-router-kv-events to
                        disable (router predicts cache state based on routing
                        decisions). env var: DYN_ROUTER_USE_KV_EVENTS |
                        default: True deprecating flag: --kv-events
  --router-replica-sync, --no-router-replica-sync
                        KV Router: Enable best-effort active-sequence
                        synchronization through the Runtime event plane. env
                        var: DYN_ROUTER_REPLICA_SYNC | default: False
  --router-track-active-blocks, --no-router-track-active-blocks, --track-active-blocks, --no-track-active-blocks
                        KV Router: Track active blocks (blocks being used for
                        ongoing generation). By default, active blocks are
                        tracked for load balancing. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_TRACK_ACTIVE_BLOCKS | default: True
                        deprecating flag: --track-active-blocks
  --router-track-output-blocks, --no-router-track-output-blocks, --track-output-blocks, --no-track-output-blocks
                        KV Router: Track output blocks during generation. When
                        enabled, the router adds placeholder blocks as tokens
                        are generated. With expected output sequence length,
                        fractional decay applies to output blocks and the
                        structurally exclusive prompt suffix; shared prompt
                        blocks retain full weight. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_TRACK_OUTPUT_BLOCKS | default: False
                        deprecating flag: --track-output-blocks
  --router-assume-kv-reuse, --no-router-assume-kv-reuse, --assume-kv-reuse, --no-assume-kv-reuse
                        KV Router: When tracking active blocks, assume KV
                        cache reuse. Use --no-router-assume-kv-reuse to
                        generate random hashes instead (when KV cache reuse is
                        not expected). env var: DYN_ROUTER_ASSUME_KV_REUSE |
                        default: True deprecating flag: --assume-kv-reuse
  --router-track-prefill-tokens, --no-router-track-prefill-tokens
                        KV Router: Include prompt-side prefill tokens in
                        active load accounting. Use --no-router-track-prefill-
                        tokens to ignore prompt tokens in router prefill-token
                        load, queue pressure, and active_prefill_tokens
                        metrics. env var: DYN_ROUTER_TRACK_PREFILL_TOKENS |
                        default: True
  --router-tracking-hash {public-xxh3-v1,keyed-xxh3-v1}
                        KV Router: Hash function for router-derived active-
                        sequence identities. env var: DYN_ROUTER_TRACKING_HASH
                        | default: public-xxh3-v1
  --router-tracking-key-file ROUTER_TRACKING_KEY_FILE
                        KV Router: File containing the 32-byte provider
                        tracking key. env var: DYN_ROUTER_TRACKING_KEY_FILE |
                        default: None
  --router-tracking-key-id ROUTER_TRACKING_KEY_ID
                        KV Router: Provider-managed tracking-key epoch
                        identifier. env var: DYN_ROUTER_TRACKING_KEY_ID |
                        default: None
  --router-prefill-load-model {none,ais}
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Prompt-side prefill load
                        model. 'none' keeps static prompt load accounting.
                        'ais' decays the oldest active prefill request using
                        AISimulate-predicted duration. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_PREFILL_LOAD_MODEL | default: none
  --router-ttl-secs ROUTER_TTL_SECS
                        KV Router: Time-to-live in seconds for blocks when KV
                        events are disabled. Only used when --no-router-kv-
                        events is set. env var: DYN_ROUTER_TTL_SECS | default:
                        120.0
  --router-approximate-cache-policy {ttl,lru}
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Retention policy for the
                        local primary approximate indexer used with --no-
                        router-kv-events. 'ttl' keeps the existing time-based
                        behavior; 'lru' uses each worker rank's advertised KV
                        capacity. Side indexers remain TTL-only. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_APPROXIMATE_CACHE_POLICY | default: ttl
  --router-queue-threshold ROUTER_QUEUE_THRESHOLD
                        --router-queue-threshold is deprecated and will be
                        removed in v1.7; use
                        policy_classes[].prefill_busy_threshold_frac in
                        --router-policy-config. KV Router: Queue threshold
                        fraction for prefill token capacity. Requests are
                        queued if all workers exceed this fraction of
                        max_num_batched_tokens. Must be >= 0. Use 0.0 for
                        maximum queueing sensitivity (queue once every
                        eligible worker has active prefill load). Unset by
                        default; setting a numeric value enables router
                        queueing. Note (SGLang backend): when --max-prefill-
                        tokens is not set, MDC's max_num_batched_tokens falls
                        back to max_total_num_tokens (the KV cache pool size),
                        not the per-step prefill window, which inflates the
                        threshold's effective denominator. Set --max-prefill-
                        tokens explicitly for predictable semantics, or use a
                        smaller threshold. env var: DYN_ROUTER_QUEUE_THRESHOLD
                        | default: None
  --router-policy-config ROUTER_POLICY_CONFIG
                        KV Router: Startup-only YAML configuration for shared
                        router settings, policy-class queues, and per-role
                        worker-selection policies. When omitted,
                        router_queue_threshold and router_queue_policy define
                        one synthetic policy class; queueing remains disabled
                        unless router_queue_threshold is set. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_POLICY_CONFIG | default: None
  --router-conditional-disagg, --no-router-conditional-disagg
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Enable conditional
                        disaggregation. When enabled, the router may bypass
                        the remote prefill step and route requests directly to
                        a decode worker. The configured policy determines
                        whether local prefill and decode is preferable for
                        each request. env var: DYN_ROUTER_CONDITIONAL_DISAGG |
                        default: False
  --router-conditional-disagg-config JSON
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: JSON object for conditional
                        disaggregation policy settings. Supported fields:
                        policy, eff_isl_threshold, eff_isl_ratio_threshold,
                        prefill_busy_threshold, decode_busy_threshold. env
                        var: DYN_ROUTER_CONDITIONAL_DISAGG_CONFIG | default:
                        None
  --router-prefill-policy ROUTER_PREFILL_POLICY
                        --router-prefill-policy is deprecated and will be
                        removed in v1.7; use worker_selection.prefill in
                        --router-policy-config. KV Router: Process-local
                        worker-selection policy type for disaggregated prefill
                        workers in this router process. Overrides
                        worker_selection.prefill from --router-policy-config.
                        Use 'default' for Dynamo's built-in worker selector.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_PREFILL_POLICY | default: None
  --router-decode-policy ROUTER_DECODE_POLICY
                        --router-decode-policy is deprecated and will be
                        removed in v1.7; use worker_selection.decode in
                        --router-policy-config. KV Router: Process-local
                        worker-selection policy type for decode workers in
                        this router process. Overrides worker_selection.decode
                        from --router-policy-config. Use 'default' for
                        Dynamo's built-in worker selector. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_DECODE_POLICY | default: None
  --router-event-threads ROUTER_EVENT_THREADS
                        KV Router: Number of KV indexer worker threads. When >
                        1, uses a concurrent radix tree with a thread pool for
                        higher throughput, including approximate routing when
                        --no-router-kv-events is set. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_EVENT_THREADS | default: 4
  --router-queue-policy {fcfs,wspt}
                        --router-queue-policy is deprecated and will be
                        removed in v1.7; use policy_classes[].queue_policy in
                        --router-policy-config. KV Router: Scheduling policy
                        for the router queue. 'fcfs' (default): first-come
                        first-served with priority bumps — optimizes tail
                        TTFT. 'wspt': weighted shortest processing time
                        (Smith's rule) — optimizes average TTFT. env var:
                        DYN_ROUTER_QUEUE_POLICY | default: fcfs
  --use-remote-indexer, --no-use-remote-indexer
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Query a remote KV indexer
                        served from the worker component via the request plane
                        instead of maintaining a local radix tree. env var:
                        DYN_USE_REMOTE_INDEXER | default: False
  --enable-session-prefix-index, --no-enable-session-prefix-index
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Track per-session block
                        lineage in a logical prefix index that outlives engine
                        cache eviction. Nothing consumes the index for routing
                        decisions yet. env var:
                        DYN_ENABLE_SESSION_PREFIX_INDEX | default: False
  --shared-cache-multiplier SHARED_CACHE_MULTIPLIER
                        --shared-cache-multiplier is deprecated and will be
                        removed in v1.7; use shared_cache_multiplier in the
                        default policy parameters in --router-policy-config.
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Multiplier for shared cache
                        hits (0.0-1.0). Blocks in the shared cache are less
                        valuable than device-local blocks. E.g. 0.5 means each
                        shared hit counts as half a device-local hit. Also
                        credits blocks a worker can fetch from a peer through
                        a KV fetch hint. The default policy uses 0.5 when
                        shared cache is enabled. env var:
                        DYN_SHARED_CACHE_MULTIPLIER | default: None
  --shared-cache-type {none,hicache}
                        [EXPERIMENTAL] KV Router: Type of external shared KV
                        cache to query. 'none' (default): disabled. 'hicache':
                        query Mooncake master directly for SGLang L3 (HiCache)
                        state using SGLang-compatible Mooncake key derivation.
                        env var: DYN_SHARED_CACHE_TYPE | default: none
  --router-predicted-ttl-secs ROUTER_PREDICTED_TTL_SECS
                        KV Router: Enable predict-on-route with this TTL in
                        seconds for entries in the local side indexer.
                        Requires KV events; omit to disable. Independent of
                        --router-ttl-secs, which covers pure approximate mode.
                        env var: DYN_ROUTER_PREDICTED_TTL_SECS | default: None
